<section image-layout="blank" id="WFFpLsjsh9" background-color="heading"><grid spacing="none"><grid-item vertical-align="center" colspan="38"><p role="eyebrow">Hegel · Ideas in motion</p><h1 font-size="40pt">What if removing every limit makes us less free?</h1><p font-size="19pt">A seminar rule says: <b>everyone may speak whenever they wish.</b> Does that free every voice—or let the strongest voices occupy the room?</p><hr color="accent" thickness="md" width="lg"/><grid divider="sm palette-5" vertical-sizing="hug"><grid-item colspan="30" padding="10pt 16pt 10pt 0"><h4>Freedom as no constraint</h4><p font-size="16pt">Nothing blocks my choice.</p></grid-item><grid-item colspan="30" padding="10pt 0 10pt 16pt"><h4>Freedom as enabled agency</h4><p font-size="16pt">Social conditions let each person speak and answer.</p></grid-item></grid><p font-size="18pt">Hegel’s wager: follow the tension until the idea returns in a richer form.</p><p font-size="sm">A focused lesson in dialectic, recognition, and social freedom</p></grid-item><grid-item padding="0" colspan="22"><img src="https://cdn-staging.gamma.app/QWjS6fBfpt/generated-images/rbAMjUxfpus2CHRTFYmKJ.png" saved-media-id="eefuemyjzr9uxe9" source="image.ai-generated" background="true" image-style="dialectical-paper-assemblage" alt="Editorial cut-paper assemblage photographed on warm ivory paper (#FAF4E8), with crisp folded planes, subtle paper fiber and long soft daylight shadows, using vermilion #A13D32, blue slate #345F67 and ochre #B3822D with carbon-black details, no text or lettering. A single vermilion paper path crosses an open adult seminar table, folds through a narrow threshold, and emerges beside two balanced blue-slate profiles." meta="{&quot;width&quot;:1248,&quot;height&quot;:1664}"></grid-item></grid></section>